eator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134071117,imgsize-134420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[16-year-old uses AI to map pollution and drive countywide policy change]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134025292.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-kelly-liu-the-16-year-old-san-jose-student-who-used-ai-to-map-dirty-air-put-pollution-sensors-in-underserved-schools-and-helped-push-a-countywide-policy-change/articleshow/134025292.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-kelly-liu-the-16-year-old-san-jose-student-who-used-ai-to-map-dirty-air-put-pollution-sensors-in-underserved-schools-and-helped-push-a-countywide-policy-change/articleshow/134025292.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134025693,imgsize-63442.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centennial Edition: Iowa press revives Ruth Suckow’s Iowa Interiors; exhibition showcases Claudia McGehee art]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133995680.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ruth Suckow's remarkable collection 'Iowa Interiors' returns in a special centennial edition, featuring captivating new illustrations by talented artist Claudia McGehee. To complement the reissue, the Hearst Center hosts an exhibition spotlighting McGehee's original artworks. This initiative not only revitalizes Suckow's literary legacy but also ensures her stories resonate with contemporary audiences, bridging Iowa's rich literary history with today's readers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1926-beekeeper-ruth-suckow-published-iowa-interiors-a-small-town-story-collection-that-made-her-nationally-known-100-years-later-a-cedar-falls-press-is-reviving-the-hard-to-find-book/articleshow/133995680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1926-beekeeper-ruth-suckow-published-iowa-interiors-a-small-town-story-collection-that-made-her-nationally-known-100-years-later-a-cedar-falls-press-is-reviving-the-hard-to-find-book/articleshow/133995680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133995749,imgsize-896445.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Skeleton Found In Roman Jar: archaeologists uncover 1,600-year-old victim; find hints of desperate escape]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133995252.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable excavation at Deultum, Bulgaria, archaeologists uncovered the remains of a young man entombed within a sizable storage jar. The evidence indicates he sought refuge there during a devastating attack, likely after the flames had already engulfed the area. His plight, frozen in time as the jar was later rebuilt over, provides a poignant glimpse into the terror and desperation of ancient times.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-man-climbed-inside-a-giant-roman-storage-jar-around-1600-years-ago-and-never-came-out-archaeologists-think-they-know-what-he-was-hiding-from/articleshow/133995252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-man-climbed-inside-a-giant-roman-storage-jar-around-1600-years-ago-and-never-came-out-archaeologists-think-they-know-what-he-was-hiding-from/articleshow/133995252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133995363,imgsize-1741162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[11-year-old inventor builds $38 moss filter that removes up to 95% of lead]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134009516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-nithya-tammana-the-11-year-old-new-jersey-inventor-who-built-a-sub-38-moss-filter-that-can-remove-up-to-95-of-lead-from-drinking-water/articleshow/134009516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/meet-nithya-tammana-the-11-year-old-new-jersey-inventor-who-built-a-sub-38-moss-filter-that-can-remove-up-to-95-of-lead-from-drinking-water/articleshow/134009516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-13T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134010002,imgsize-63790.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Deer Learn To Ignore Deterrents: Human shouts scare best; habituation soon blunts effect]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133992150.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Research indicates that loud human noises and bright lights were effective in driving deer and elk away from crops, while predator sounds and dog barks didn’t have the same effect. Over a period of six weeks, these animals became accustomed to the deterrents, especially those near human activity. Researchers recommend diversifying stimuli and introducing consequences to keep these animals from adapting.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-played-human-shouts-wolf-and-cougar-calls-near-british-columbia-crop-fields-deer-fled-64-of-the-time-from-human-voices-but-quickly-learned-to-ignore-the-deterrents/articleshow/133992150.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/scientists-played-human-shouts-wolf-and-cougar-calls-near-british-columbia-crop-fields-deer-fled-64-of-the-time-from-human-voices-but-quickly-learned-to-ignore-the-deterrents/articleshow/133992150.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133992270,imgsize-1164978.cms"/></item></channel></rss>